# Cloudflare Pages routing. Mirrors the SPA rewrite from vercel.json.
#
# Anything without a file extension is an application route (/mcp, deep links
# into panels), so it has to resolve to the shell rather than 404. Requests
# that DO carry an extension fall through to the static asset, which is why
# this cannot simply be `/* /index.html 200`.
#
# Note the bSDD proxy that vercel.json provides has no equivalent here:
# `_redirects` can only proxy same-origin paths, so /api/bsdd/* needs a Pages
# Function. Until one exists, bSDD classification lookups are unavailable on a
# Pages deployment — every other feature is unaffected.

/mcp     /index.html   200
/mcp/*   /index.html   200
/*       /index.html   200
